    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "act": "FALSIFIABILITY",
      "narration_text": "And that explains things people find strange. Ask a model to count letters in a word and it can stumble, because it never saw the letters, only pieces. Prices and context limits are counted in tokens. And languages that were rarer in the training text get split into more pieces, so they cost more to process.",
